  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "We measured liver transcripts, proteins and metabolites in the same 50 mice, each as a complete continuous table. I'd like one partial-correlation network linking the transcript and protein layers, and a second network that models all three layers together in a single fit."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"one partial-correlation network linking the transcript and protein layers\" -- available from DRAGON.\n2. \"a second network that models all three layers together in a single fit\" -- not matched to any registered workflow.\n\n**DRAGON**. DRAGON fits a two-layer Gaussian graphical model with layer-aware shrinkage. Partial correlations describe associations conditional on the other measured features under that model; they are not directed causal effects. The two omics layers must refer to matched samples.\n\nYou would need DRAGON omics layer 1, DRAGON omics layer 2. The analysis would provide inferred associations between omics features.\n\nFor “partial-correlation network linking the transcript and protein layers”, no registered workflow meets the stated requirement. That part needs a clearer measurement or an external method.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran.\n\nWhat measurement would let you distinguish the remaining explanation?"
    }
  ],
